CHAPTER XIV PROHIBITIONS
Article 54
a. treating Women and Children in a discriminatory manner that results in Women and Children experiencing losses, both material and moral, thereby hindering their social function;
b. treating persons with disabilities in a discriminatory manner;
c. placing, leaving, involving, ordering the involvement of Women and Children with disabilities in situations of maltreatment and neglect;
d. placing, leaving, committing, ordering the commission of or participating in committing Violence against Women and Children;
e. committing Violence or threat of Violence to force Women and Children to have sexual intercourse with him/her or with another person;
f. committing Violence or threat of violence, forcing, committing deceit, committing a series of lies, or persuading Women and Children to commit or allow obscene acts to be committed; g. placing, leaving, committing, ordering the commission of or participating in committing kidnapping, sale and/or trafficking of Women and Children; h. obstructing Women and Children from enjoying their own culture, acknowledging and practicing their religious teachings and/or using their own language without neglecting access to Community development and culture; i. placing, leaving, committing, ordering the commission of or participating in committing economic and/or sexual exploitation against Women and Children; j. intentionally placing, leaving, involving Women and Children in the abuse, as well as production and distribution of narcotics and/or psychotropic substances; and/or
k. intentionally placing, leaving, involving, ordering the involvement of Women and Children in the abuse, as well as production and distribution of alcohol and other addictive substances.

